<title>POLAND: Polish registered trade gap up to $3.56 bln in Q1.</title>
<headline>Polish registered trade gap up to $3.56 bln in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's registered trade gap, based on customs receipts, amounted to $3.56 billion in the first quarter of 1997, 58 percent more than in the same period of 1996, the Central Statistical Office (GUS) said on Friday.</p>
<p>According to central bank figures, based on current account flows, Poland had a merchandise trade deficit of $3.07 billion in the January-March period.</p>
<p> POLISH TRADE BALANCE (MLN USD)   Q1 1997	  Q1 1996</p>
<p> Trade balance			  -3,555	   -2,250</p>
<p> Exports				   6,051	    5,950</p>
<p> Imports				   9,606	    8,196</p>
